The bug was a classic off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was accessing `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError since there was no second element

I fixed it by changing `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`, and now all tests pass successfully.
